<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- Team chat (Chat mode, workspaces, channels and direct messages). Each name maps a desktop catalog key
     (src/i18n/en.js, chat.* and agent.empty.*Chat) by the rule of the chat contract: dots and hyphens become
     underscores and camelCase becomes snake_case, so chat.sidebar.rowUnread is chat_sidebar_row_unread.
     {placeholders} become %1$s, %2$s in the order they first appear in the English text; {count} becomes %d in
     a plural with no other placeholder, and %N$d beside others. Plural keys become <plurals> with one and other.
     The texts are the desktop's, except where the desktop says "this computer": there it says "this phone",
     marked phone wording. A few texts name a desktop keyboard shortcut; they stay as the desktop has them.
     The Android-only names at the end have no desktop key. ChatStringsTest checks this file against values-nl. -->
<resources>

